                <pb facs="0309" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg819"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>In telegram 438, April 14, 1:51 p. m., from New York, Mr. Ross sent to Mr. Rusk
                    the informal, written comments of the Jewish Agency <pb facs="0310" n="820"
                        xml:id="pg820"/> on the American 15-point trusteeship program for Palestine.
                    The telegram noted that Mr. Ross had received the comments the night before. At
                    one point in the 14-page telegram, appeared the following Jewish Agency comment:
                    “It is because the very concept of trusteeship is so flagrantly out of accord
                    with the general principles and current realities of the Palestine situation
                    that no improvement of the US proposals can make them a useful starting point in
                    the quest for a political settlement.” (501.BB Palestine/4–1448)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
